WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.060
The basket arrives before the

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.320
officer does.

3
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.760
Sweets, dry fruits, a satin

4
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.760
ribbon, and a card that says:

5
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.010
no obligation.

6
00:00:09.822 --> 00:00:11.522
Nothing says obligation quite

7
00:00:11.522 --> 00:00:14.102
like the words, no obligation.

8
00:00:14.102 --> 00:00:16.162
This is a made up case.

9
00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:18.142
Anita buys supplies for a

10
00:00:18.142 --> 00:00:19.782
government office, and the

11
00:00:19.782 --> 00:00:21.402
basket is from a contractor

12
00:00:21.402 --> 00:00:23.172
whose bills she signs.

13
00:00:23.751 --> 00:00:25.411
It is festival season.

14
00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:27.411
The sweets look excellent.

15
00:00:27.411 --> 00:00:29.211
The whole office is already

16
00:00:29.211 --> 00:00:30.641
looking at the ribbon.

17
00:00:31.253 --> 00:00:32.213
The dilemma:

18
00:00:32.213 --> 00:00:34.913
can Anita accept a gift from a

19
00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:36.953
man whose bills she approves,

20
00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:38.793
and still judge those bills

21
00:00:38.793 --> 00:00:39.643
fairly?

22
00:00:40.327 --> 00:00:41.187
Option A:

23
00:00:41.187 --> 00:00:42.007
keep it.

24
00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:43.787
It is only sweets.

25
00:00:43.787 --> 00:00:45.167
Option B:

26
00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.787
keep it, and share it around the

27
00:00:46.787 --> 00:00:49.027
office. Option C:

28
00:00:49.027 --> 00:00:50.767
send it back politely, and

29
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.547
record why in writing.

30
00:00:52.547 --> 00:00:54.557
Pause here, and choose.

31
00:00:55.238 --> 00:00:56.698
Option A calls the gift

32
00:00:56.698 --> 00:00:58.578
harmless. But a gift from

33
00:00:58.578 --> 00:01:00.198
someone with official dealings

34
00:01:00.198 --> 00:01:01.978
is just what Rule thirteen is

35
00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:02.968
written for.

36
00:01:03.524 --> 00:01:05.944
Option B spreads the sweets, not

37
00:01:05.944 --> 00:01:06.824
the problem.

38
00:01:06.824 --> 00:01:08.624
The basket was still accepted,

39
00:01:08.624 --> 00:01:10.814
and the contractor knows it.

40
00:01:11.229 --> 00:01:13.349
Option C follows the spirit of

41
00:01:13.349 --> 00:01:14.669
Rule thirteen:

42
00:01:14.669 --> 00:01:16.149
no gifts from those with

43
00:01:16.149 --> 00:01:17.429
official dealings.

44
00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:19.879
Return it, and leave a record.

45
00:01:20.522 --> 00:01:22.602
A sound answer returns the gift,

46
00:01:22.602 --> 00:01:24.582
records it in writing, judges

47
00:01:24.582 --> 00:01:26.722
the bills on merit, and does not

48
00:01:26.722 --> 00:01:27.952
fear scrutiny.

49
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:30.250
For GS4:

50
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.990
a gift is never just a gift,

51
00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.310
when the giver has a file on

52
00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.160
your desk.

53
00:01:37.045 --> 00:01:38.745
The basket goes back with a

54
00:01:38.745 --> 00:01:39.845
polite note.

55
00:01:39.845 --> 00:01:41.805
The office assistant takes it

56
00:01:41.805 --> 00:01:43.915
harder than the contractor does.
